        "original_id": "23cd25ba-01a9-5b0f-9cf4-2b7a0c5814e7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Mulligan, Hasan Akbar, Nidal Malik Hasan\n- Roles: Prosecutor, United States Army soldier\n- Organizations: United States Army\n- Events: November 2009 Fort Hood shooting, United States invasion of Iraq\n- Places: Camp Pennsylvania, Kuwait\n- Legal Cases: United States v. Hasan K. Akbar, courts-martial of Hasan Akbar and Nidal Malik Hasan\n\nFacts:\n- On March 23, 2003, Hasan Akbar, a United States Army soldier, carried out a premeditated attack at Camp Pennsylvania in Kuwait during the start of the United States invasion of Iraq.\n- United States v. Hasan K. Akbar was the court-martial of Hasan Akbar for the March 23, 2003 attack at Camp Pennsylvania in Kuwait.\n- In November 2009, Nidal Malik Hasan was the sole accused in the Fort Hood shooting.\n- Colonel Michael Mulligan is a prosecutor in the United States Army.\n- Michael Mulligan served as the lead prosecutor in the courts-martial of Hasan Akbar and Nidal Malik Hasan.",
